  "attempt": "For an accelerated odd Collatz valuation word a_1,...,a_m, let A_r be the sum of its last r valuations and put Phi=sum_(r=1)^m 3^(r-1)/2^(A_r). Then Phi=C/2^S exactly and, when 2^S>3^m, the affine descent threshold is theta=C/(2^S-3^m)=Phi/(1-3^m/2^S). Every realizing odd start n descends after this prefix exactly when n>theta. The TICKET-154 floor-two suffix condition A_r>=2r is sufficient because it forces theta<=1, but it is not necessary: the realized word (1,1,2,3) sends 7 to 5 while its full suffix sum is 7<8.",
